Since I upgraded to 2.6.27-r7 or 2.6.27-r8 (from 2.6.26-r4) I don't have ne=
ither net=2C nor usb=2C nor sound.
For net in particular=2C when I bring up the interface I get an error somet=
hing like this:=20
SIOCCFLAGS ERROR: Device or ressource busy.
=20
Looking in dmesg=2C I've seen that after my ide2 takes IRQ11=2C all the mod=
ules for my network card (8139too)=2C usb (uhci-hcd) and sound (snd-cs4236)=
 complain that they can't assign an interrupt (IRQ11).
=20
I've included all files relevant to my computer in the bzip2 tar file attac=
hed (kernel config=2C dmesg=2C lspci=2C /proc/{interrupts=2Cioports=2Ciomem=
=2Ccpuinfo=2Cirq/}.
I've also tried to start with kernel parametters irqpoll and irqfixup=2C th=
inking it might help. It still didn't work=2C and I included the dmesg obta=
ined in the attach.
=20
If anyone could give me a hint about what's going on=2C and how I can fix i=
t=2C I'd be very grateful.
=20
In case that matters=2C I'm running gentoo as distribution.
Thanks for any help!
